  {
   "caption": "The ∀ part survives: every choice of v, w from {2, 4, 6} was already one of the choices in the big world, and a quantifier-free body without functions only looks at those elements.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "note2",
     "set": {
      "text": "fewer cases for ∀v∀w: still true",
      "tone": "success"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "So a model with at most 3 elements exists (GATE 2018, option A). With function symbols, or a ∀ before an ∃, a needed element could be outside the kept set.",
